ed_sale_price must estimate the NEW lot across possible grades, not copy a current C-grade unit quote. Use grade-specific evidence and the explicit mixture priors; anchors are unvalidated. Estimate continuation_value per unsold new unit after this horizon: uncertain net future sale revenue before expiry, after grade decay and future costs. It is NOT a market buyback and is not guaranteed. Set zero if unsupported; it is capped at expected purchase cost. Do not assume a still-saleable unit is physically discarded merely because this short planning horizon ends. Missing observations are UNKNOWN, not zero demand. demand.json lists categories without demand weights. The market end is a hard cash-realization deadline. Limit the forecast horizon to hours_to_end minus two hours if shorter, and do not assign terminal value to unsold stock. The operator prefers active capital turnover with positive acquisition spread, revenue and honest buyer satisfaction over idle cash or extreme per-sale markups. Ranking weights apply to percentiles, not raw units."}}
